  "id": "Compound::DB00622 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Nicardipine is linked to Cyp2e1 through a series of molecular and metabolic pathways that involve the enzyme Cyp2c19. The evidence suggests that Nicardipine, as a member of the dihydropyridine class, interacts with Cyp2c19, which in turn participates in the oxidation of arachidonic acid, an activity that is also performed by Cyp2e1. This implies a potential metabolic pathway where Nicardipine may influence the activity of Cyp2e1 through its interaction with Cyp2c19, possibly by modulating the enzyme's expression or activity. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Nicardipine to Cyp2e1, including through different members of the dihydropyridine family, highlights a broader role in the metabolic regulation of Cyp2e1. The integration of these pathways suggests that Nicardipine may exert a regulatory effect on Cyp2e1 through a mechanism involving the arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity, which is a key step in the metabolism of various substrates. This mechanism is further supported by the shared involvement of Cyp2e1 in the metabolic processes of different substrates, indicating a possible functional overlap in the pathways regulated by Nicardipine.",
